// The Moonbean Cafe: Luna's five visits, in order, whenever Kai goes, and a
// short hello after the fifth. Every visit costs a $5 coffee.
//
// 1 "First time here?"   2 the city (the stars, Tuesday's hint)
// 3 the sketchbook (ask, don't grab: Wednesday's hint)   4 the rainy evening
// 5 the ask: yes with affection >= 3, then the $20 tickets (Thursday's hint),
//   or her number on the cup without the money.
// Lines: visit k at k01.., the hello at 601..; menu k is visit k's choice.

str caf101a
    en "The door bell rings. Inside, the cafe smells of cinnamon and warm milk."
str caf102a
    en "Welcome! First time here? I'd love to know what I can get for you."
str caf103a
    en "Up close she is even prettier. Her name tag says LUNA. Kai's mind goes blank."
str c1a
    en "I'll just have a black coffee."
str c1b
    en "What do you recommend?"
str c1c
    en "Do you come here often?"
str caf111a
    en "One black coffee, coming up. Simple. I respect that."
str caf121a
    en "Ooh, nobody ever asks! The honey lavender latte. My favourite. I invented it, actually."
str caf122a
    en "Then I'll have that. Your favourite."
str caf123a
    en "...Good choice."
str caf131a
    en "I... work here? So, yes. Every day, actually."
str caf132a
    en "(Smooth, Kai. Very smooth.)"
str caf141a
    en "I'm Luna, by the way. You're the new boy at Sato House, right? I saw the van."
str caf142a
    en "Kai. Yes. Mrs. Sato's building. Or Mochi's, apparently."
str caf143a
    en "Ha! Mochi really is the boss. See you around, Kai."

str caf201a
    en "Kai! Back again? The usual... wait, do you have a usual yet?"
str caf202a
    en "Not yet. Surprise me."
str caf203a
    en "So. How do you like Kaminato so far? Be honest."
str c2a
    en "The food here is amazing."
str c2b
    en "The stars over the harbour."
str c2c
    en "Honestly? I miss home a bit."
str caf211a
    en "Right? The ramen place by the station is dangerous. I go twice a week."
str caf221a
    en "The stars? You noticed them too?"
str caf222a
    en "From the pier you can see the whole summer triangle. I go there after closing."
str caf223a
    en "Maybe you could show me which one is Vega."
str caf224a
    en "...Maybe I could."
str caf231a
    en "That's okay. It took me a whole year to stop missing my mom's cooking."
str caf232a
    en "Come here when it gets bad. Coffee helps. A little."
str caf241a
    en "She hands him his cup. There is a tiny star drawn in the foam."

str caf301a
    en "On her break, Luna sits at the corner table with a pencil behind her ear, drawing in a worn sketchbook."
str caf302a
    en "Oh! Kai. Sorry, I'm on my break. Ken will take your order."
str c3a
    en "What are you drawing?"
str c3b
    en "Can I see? Come on, show me."
str c3c
    en "Shouldn't you be working?"
str caf311a
    en "Just... the view from the window. The street lamps, the people going home."
str caf312a
    en "You can look, if you want. Since you asked nicely."
str caf313a
    en "The page is full of tiny lights and tiny people. It's beautiful."
str caf314a
    en "You're really good, Luna."
str caf321a
    en "Um... not today. It's not ready."
str caf322a
    en "She closes the sketchbook and holds it against her apron."
str caf323a
    en "(Daichi literally told me not to do that.)"
str caf331a
    en "It's my break. Breaks are for the things I love."
str caf332a
    en "...Sorry. That came out sharp. Enjoy your coffee."

str caf401a
    en "Rain pours over Hikari Street. The cafe is empty except for the two of them."
str caf402a
    en "You're soaked! Sit, sit. Nobody else is coming in this weather."
str caf403a
    en "Can I tell you a secret? I want to make picture books. Stars, foxes, lost kids finding their way home. That kind of thing."
str caf404a
    en "My parents think it's a waste of time. Maybe they're right."
str c4a
    en "Do it. I'd buy the first copy."
str c4b
    en "Picture books? Like, for babies?"
str c4c
    en "Anyway... can I get a refill?"
str caf411a
    en "You'd really... buy it?"
str caf412a
    en "I'd make Mrs. Sato buy ten. And Mochi."
str caf413a
    en "Thank you, Kai. Really."
str caf421a
    en "...Yeah. For babies. Never mind."
str caf431a
    en "Oh. Sure. One refill, coming up."
str caf441a
    en "The rain softens. For a while neither of them says anything, and it's nice."

str caf501a
    en "Kai! You look nervous. Did something happen?"
str caf502a
    en "N-no! I mean... the Star Festival is this Saturday, at the hill observatory."
str c5a
    en "Would you go with me?"
str c5b
    en "...I just wanted to tell you. Bye!"
str caf511a
    en "Oh... Kai, that's sweet. But I promised my aunt I'd help at her food stall."
str caf512a
    en "Maybe... another time?"
str caf513a
    en "It doesn't sound like another time."
str caf521a
    en "Me? With you?"
str caf522a
    en "...I'd love to."
str caf531a
    en "Great! Then I'll get us two tickets. My treat."
str caf532a
    en "It's a date, then. Saturday, seven o'clock, at the bottom of the hill."
str caf541a
    en "Kai reaches for his wallet. Not even enough for one ticket."
str caf542a
    en "Luna, I'm so sorry. I... can't afford the tickets this week."
str caf543a
    en "Hey. It's okay."
str caf544a
    en "She takes a marker and writes something on his paper cup."
str caf545a
    en "My number. Next time, for sure. Okay?"
str caf551a
    en "Kai? ...Wait!"
str caf552a
    en "Too late. Kai is already halfway down Hikari Street, red to the ears."

str caf601a
    en "Only one more sleep! I already picked my yukata."
str caf602a
    en "Did you save my number? ...Good. Don't lose it."
str caf603a
    en "Hi, Kai. The usual?"

ui sCafe modal=false
    if dlg::line == 101
        text caf101a pos=252,827 width=1440 tint=0.78,0.86,1,1
